hadiths[52]{hadithnumber,text}:
"20001","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from Matar, from Abdullah ibn Buraydah al-Aslami who said: Ubaydullah ibn Ziyad doubted concerning the Hawd (Pool), so he sent for Abu Barzah al-Aslami and he came to him. The companions of Ubaydullah said to him: The amir only sent for you to ask you about the Hawd, did you hear anything concerning it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mention it: whoever denies it, may Allah not give him to drink from it."
"20002","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Sulayman al-Taymi informed us, from Sayyar Abu al-Minhal, from Abu Barzah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in the morning prayer from sixty to a hundred (verses)."
"20003","Mu'tamir narrated to us, he said: my father informed me, from Abu al-Minhal, from Abu Barzah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in the morning prayer from a hundred to sixty and from sixty to a hundred."
"20004","Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Sulayman, from Abu Uthman, from Abu Barzah who said: There was a riding camel, or a she-camel, or a camel carrying some of the people's goods, and on it was a slave girl. They took a path between two mountains and the road became narrow for them. She saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Hal, hal, O Allah, curse it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who is the owner of this slave girl? Let no riding camel, or she-camel, or camel carrying any part of the curse of Allah, the Blessed and Exalted, accompany us."
"20005","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Awf narrated to us, Abu al-Minhal narrated to me, he said: I went with my father to Abu Barzah al-Aslami, and my father said to him: Narrate to us how the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray the obligatory prayer. He said: He used to pray al-Hajir, which is the one you call the first, when the sun declined, and he would pray Asr and one of us would return to his lodging in Madinah while the sun was still alive. He said: And I forgot what he said about Maghrib. He used to prefer to delay Isha, and he used to dislike sleep before it and talk after it. He would finish the morning prayer when one of us could recognize his companion, and he would recite from sixty to a hundred."
"20006","Yahya ibn Sa'id and Waki' narrated to us, they said: Aban ibn Sam'ah narrated to us, from Abu al-Wazi', from Abu Barzah who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, teach me something I may benefit from. He said: Remove harm from the path of the Muslims."
"20007","Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Hajjaj informed us, from Abu Hashim al-Wasiti, from Rufay' Abu al-Aliyah, from Abu Barzah al-Aslami who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would, latterly, when the sitting grew long and he stood up, say: Glory be to You, O Allah, and with Your praise, I bear witness that there is no god but You, I seek Your forgiveness and repent to You. One of us said to him: These are words we did not used to hear from you before. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is an expiation for what occurs in the sitting."
"20008","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Azraq ibn Qays who said: Abu Barzah was in al-Ahwaz on the bank of a river, holding the bridle in his hand while praying, and the mount began to retreat and he began to move back with it. A man from the Khawarij began to say: O Allah, disgrace this old man, how he prays. When he prayed, he said: I heard what you said. I went on campaigns with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) six, or seven, or eight times, and I witnessed his command and his facilitation. My going back with my mount was easier for me than leaving it so it would run to its home and cause hardship for me. And Abu Barzah prayed Asr two rak'ahs."
"20009","Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us, Mahdi ibn Maymun narrated to us, Jabir Abu al-Wazi' narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Barzah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a man to a tribe of the Arabs, and they beat him and insulted him. He returned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and complained of that to him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Had you gone to the people of Oman, they would not have beaten you nor insulted you."
"20010","Yunus narrated to us, Abu al-Ashhab narrated to us, from Ali ibn al-Hakam, from Abu Barzah al-Aslami who said: Abu al-Ashhab said: I only know it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Indeed among what I fear for you are the lusts of error in your bellies and your private parts, and the misleading trials."
"20011","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Ashhab informed us, from Abu al-Hakam al-Bunani, from Abu Barzah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Indeed among what I fear for you are the lusts of error in your bellies and your private parts, and the misleading desires."
"20012","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from al-Mughirah ibn Abi Barzah, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Aslam, may Allah grant them safety, and Ghifar, may Allah forgive them. I did not say it, but Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, said it."
"20013","Hajjaj narrated to us, Shu'bah informed us, from Abu Hamzah, their neighbor, he said: I heard Humayd ibn Hilal narrate, from Abdullah ibn Mutarrif, from Abu Barzah who said: The most hateful people, or the most hateful tribes, to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) were Thaqif and Banu Hanifah."
"20014","Aswad ibn Amir Shadhan narrated to us, Abu Bakr, meaning Ibn Ayyash, informed us, from al-A'mash, from Sa'id ibn Abdullah ibn Jurayj, from Abu Barzah al-Aslami who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O company of those who believed with their tongues while faith did not enter their hearts, do not backbite the Muslims and do not follow their faults, for whoever follows their faults, Allah will follow his fault, and whoever has Allah follow his fault, He will disgrace him in his house."
"20015","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Sukayn narrated to us, Sayyar ibn Salamah narrated to us, he heard Abu Barzah raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The rulers are from Quraysh: when mercy is sought from them they show mercy, when they covenant they fulfill, and when they judge they are just. Whoever of them does not do that, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people."
"20016","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Kinanah ibn Nu'aym al-Adawi, from Abu Barzah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in one of his campaigns, and when he finished fighting he said: Do you miss anyone? They said: O Messenger of Allah, we miss so-and-so and so-and-so. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: But I miss Julaybib, so seek him. They sought him and found him beside seven whom he had killed and who then killed him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and stood over him and said: He killed seven and then they killed him, this one is of me and I am of him, he killed seven and they killed him, this one is of me and I am of him. He was lifted to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he placed him on his forearm, and he had no bed except the forearms of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until he buried him, and he did not mention washing."
"20017","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Mihzam al-Abdi informed us, from Abu Talut al-Abdi who said: I heard Abu Barzah, as he came out from Ubaydullah ibn Ziyad angry, say: I did not think I would live until I remained among a people who reproach me for the companionship of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). They said: This Muhammad of yours is short and stocky. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) speak about the Hawd: whoever denies it, may Allah, the Blessed and Exalted, not give him to drink from it."
"20018","Abdullah ibn Muhammad narrated to us, and I heard it myself from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Shaybah, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Sulayman ibn Amr ibn al-Ahwas who said: The master of this house, Abu Hilal, informed me, he said: I heard Abu Barzah say: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, and he heard two men singing, one answering the other, saying: His young companions will remain with their bones showing, war has kept him from being buried in a grave. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: See who they are. They said: So-and-so and so-and-so. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, overturn them with a crash and thrust them into the Fire with a thrust."
"20019","Abd al-Wahhab ibn Abd al-Majid narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from Abu al-Minhal, from Abu Barzah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to dislike sleep before Isha and did not like talk after it."
"20020","Affan narrated to us, Sukayn ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Sayyar ibn Salamah Abu al-Minhal narrated to us, he said: I entered with my father upon Abu Barzah, and in my ears that day were earrings, and I was a boy. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The rulers are from Quraysh, three times: as long as they do three things: when they judge they are just, when mercy is sought they show mercy, and when they covenant they fulfill. Whoever of them does not do that, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people."
"20021","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, al-Azraq ibn Qays informed us, from Sharik ibn Shihab who said: I used to wish to meet a man from the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who would narrate to me about the Khawarij. I met Abu Barzah on the day of Arafah among some of his companions and said: O Abu Barzah, narrate to us something you heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say about the Khawarij. He said: I will narrate to you what my ears heard and my eyes saw. Dinars were brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he was distributing them, and with him was a black man with trimmed hair, wearing two white garments, with a mark of prostration between his eyes. He confronted the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), coming to him from the front, but he gave him nothing. Then he came to him from behind and he gave him nothing. He said: By Allah, O Muhammad, you have not been just today in the division. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) became intensely angry, then said: By Allah, you will not find after me anyone more just toward you than me. He said it three times. Then he said: There will come out from the east men of whom this one was a type, their guidance is like this: they recite the Quran but it does not pass their throats, they pass through the religion as the arrow passes through the game, they do not return to it. And he placed his hand on his chest. Their mark is shaving. They will continue to come out until the last of them comes out. When you see them, kill them. He said it three times. The worst of creation and creatures. He said it three times. And Hammad said: They do not return to it."
"20022","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Kinanah ibn Nu'aym al-Adawi, from Abu Barzah al-Aslami, that Julaybib was a man who would enter upon women, passing by them and joking with them. I said to my wife: Julaybib shall not enter upon you, for if he enters upon you I will surely do such-and-such. He said: The Ansar, when one of them had an unmarried woman, would not marry her off until they knew whether the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had any need concerning her or not. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to a man from the Ansar: Marry your daughter to me. He said: Gladly and as an honor, O Messenger of Allah, and the delight of my eye. He said: I do not want her for myself. He said: For whom, O Messenger of Allah? He said: For Julaybib. He said: O Messenger of Allah, I will consult her mother. He went to her mother and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) proposes your daughter. She said: Gladly and the delight of my eye. He said: He is not proposing her for himself, he is proposing her for Julaybib. She said: Julaybib, fie! Julaybib, fie! Julaybib, fie! No, by Allah, she shall not marry him. When he was about to stand to go to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to inform him of what her mother said, the girl said: Who proposed me to you? Her mother told her. She said: Do you reject the command of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? Hand me over, for he will not let me be lost. Her father went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him. He said: Deal with her accordingly, so he married her to Julaybib. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out on one of his campaigns, and when Allah granted him booty, he said to his Companions: Do you miss anyone? They said: We miss so-and-so and we miss so-and-so. He said: See, do you miss anyone? They said: No. He said: But I miss Julaybib, so seek him among the slain. They sought him and found him beside seven whom he had killed and who then killed him. They said: O Messenger of Allah, here he is beside seven whom he had killed and who then killed him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to him and stood over him and said: He killed seven and they killed him, this one is of me and I am of him, this one is of me and I am of him, two or three times. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placed him on his forearms, and a grave was dug for him, and he had no bed except the forearms of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then he placed him in his grave, and it was not mentioned that he washed him. Thabit said: There was no unmarried woman among the Ansar more abundantly provided for than her. Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah narrated to Thabit, he said: Do you know what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplicated for her? He said: O Allah, pour good upon her abundantly and do not make her life toilsome. He said: There was no unmarried woman among the Ansar more abundantly provided for than her. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: No one in the world narrated it except Hammad ibn Salamah, how excellent a hadith it is."
"20023","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Abu Bakr, meaning Ibn Shu'ayb ibn al-Habhab, narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu al-Wazi' Jabir al-Rasibi mention that Abu Barzah narrated to him, he said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I said: O Messenger of Allah, I do not know, perhaps you will pass away and I will remain after you, so narrate to me something by which Allah will benefit me. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Do such-and-such, do such-and-such, I have forgotten that, and remove harm from the path."
"20024","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Uyaynah informed us, from his father, from Abu Barzah al-Aslami who said: I went out one day walking, and there was the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heading toward me. I thought he intended to relieve himself, so I withdrew from him and crossed his path. He saw me and motioned to me, so I came to him and he took my hand, and we walked together. We came upon a man praying, doing much bowing and prostration. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you see him showing off? I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He released my hand, then joined his palms together and raised them level with his shoulders and lowered them, saying: Upon you is a moderate, right course, three times, for whoever overburdens the religion will be overcome by it. Yazid said in Baghdad: Buraydah al-Aslami, though he had said: from Abu Barzah, then he returned to Buraydah."
"20025","Waki' and Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, they said: Buraydah al-Aslami."
"20026","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Abu al-Ashhab informed us, from Abu al-Hakam al-Bunani, from Abu Barzah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Indeed among what I fear for you are the lusts of error in your bellies and your private parts, and the misleading desires."
"20027","Yazid narrated to us, Abu Hilal al-Rasibi Muhammad ibn Sulaym informed us, from Abu al-Wazi', from Abu Barzah who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, teach me something by which Allah, the Blessed and Exalted, will benefit me. He said: Look at what harms people and remove it from their path."
"20028","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from al-Taymi, and Yazid narrated to us, he said: al-Taymi informed us, from Abu Uthman, from Abu Barzah, Yazid said: al-Aslami, who said: There was a riding camel, or a she-camel, or a camel carrying goods of some people, and they took a path between two mountains, and on it was a slave girl, and the road became narrow for them. She saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and began to say: Hal, hal, O Allah, curse it, or curse him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let no she-camel, or riding camel, or camel carrying the curse of Allah, the Blessed and Exalted, accompany me."
"20029","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Shu'bah, al-Azraq ibn Qays narrated to me, he said: I saw an old man in al-Ahwaz praying Asr with his mount's bridle in his hand. It kept moving back and he kept stepping back with it, while a man sitting from the Khawarij insulted him. When he prayed, he said: I heard what you said. I went on campaigns with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) six, or seven campaigns, and I witnessed his command and his facilitation. I would return with my mount with me, dearer to me than leaving it to go to its home and cause hardship for me. He said: I said: How much did he pray? He said: Two rak'ahs. And behold, he was Abu Barzah."
"20030","Waki' narrated to us, Aban ibn Sam'ah narrated to us, from Abu al-Wazi' al-Rasibi, from Abu Barzah al-Aslami who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, guide me to a deed that will admit me to Paradise, or by which I may benefit. He said: Remove harm from the path of the Muslims."
"20031","Waki' narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to me, he said: I heard Abu al-Minhal, from Abu Barzah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade sleep before it and talk after it."
"20032","Waki' narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Khalid, from Abu al-Minhal, from Abu Barzah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite between sixty and a hundred, meaning in the morning prayer."
"20033","Isma'il narrated to us, Shaddad ibn Sa'id narrated to me, Jabir ibn Amr al-Rasibi narrated to me, he said: I heard Abu Barzah al-Aslami say: I killed Abd al-Uzza ibn Khatal while he was clinging to the cover of the Ka'bah. And I said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): O Messenger of Allah, command me with a deed to do. He said: Remove harm from the path, for it is charity for you."
"20034","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Awf narrated to us, from Abu al-Minhal who said: My father said to me: Go to Abu Barzah al-Aslami. I went with him until we entered upon him in his house while he sat in the shade of an upper room of reeds. We sat with him on a very hot day, and my father asked him: Narrate to me how the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray the obligatory prayer. He said: He used to pray al-Hajir, which you call the first, when the sun declined, and he used to pray Asr, then one of us would return to his lodging in the farthest part of Madinah while the sun was still alive. He said: And I forgot what he said about Maghrib. He said: He used to prefer to delay Isha, which you call al-Atamah. He said: He used to dislike sleep before it and talk after it. He said: He would finish the morning prayer when one of us could recognize his companion, and he would recite from sixty to a hundred."
"20035","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Awf narrated to us, from Musawir ibn Ubayd who said: I came to Abu Barzah and said: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stone? He said: Yes, a man from us called Ma'iz ibn Malik. My father said: Rawh said: Musawir ibn Ubayd al-Himmani."
"20036","Affan narrated to us, Mahdi ibn Maymun narrated to us, Abu al-Wazi', a man from Banu Rasib, narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Barzah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a messenger to a tribe of the Arabs concerning something, Mahdi does not know what it was. He said: They insulted him and beat him, and he complained of that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Had you gone to the people of Oman, they would not have insulted you nor beaten you."
"20037","Yunus narrated to us, Mahdi narrated to us, Jabir Abu al-Wazi' narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Barzah narrate from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a messenger to a tribe of the Arabs, and he mentioned the like of it."
"20038","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Sayyar ibn Salamah, from Abu Barzah al-Aslami, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to delay the last Isha until a third of the night, and he used to dislike sleep before it and talk after it. He used to recite in Fajr between a hundred and sixty, and he would finish when one of us could recognize the face of another."
"20039","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Qutbah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from a man of Basra, from Abu Barzah al-Aslami who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called out until he made the maidens hear, and said: O company of those who believed with their tongues while faith did not enter their hearts, do not backbite the Muslims and do not follow their faults, for whoever follows the fault of his brother, Allah will follow his fault until He disgraces him in his house."
"20040","Abu Sa'id narrated to us, Shaddad Abu Talhah narrated to us, Jabir ibn Amr Abu al-Wazi' narrated to us, from Abu Barzah who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, command me with a deed to do. He said: Remove harm from the path, for it is charity for you."
"20041","He said: And I killed Abd al-Uzza ibn Khatal while he was clinging to the cover of the Ka'bah. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of the conquest of Makkah: The people are safe, except Abd al-Uzza ibn Khatal."
"20042","And I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: I have a Hawd (Pool) between Aylah and Sanaa, its width like its length, in it are two spouts pouring from Paradise, one of silver and the other of gold, sweeter than honey, cooler than snow, and whiter than milk. Whoever drinks from it will not thirst until he enters Paradise. In it are pitchers as numerous as the stars of the sky."
"20043","al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Sukayn ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Sayyar ibn Salamah Abu al-Minhal al-Riyahi who said: I entered with my father upon Abu Barzah al-Aslami, and in my ears that day were earrings, and I was a boy. He said: Abu Barzah said: I praise Allah that I have come to blame this tribe of Quraysh: so-and-so here fights for the world, and so-and-so here fights for the world, meaning Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan. He said: Until he mentioned Ibn al-Azraq. He said: Then he said: The most beloved people to me are this band, unkempt and thin-bellied from the wealth of the Muslims, with backs light from their blood. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The rulers are from Quraysh, the rulers are from Quraysh, the rulers are from Quraysh. I have a right over them and they have a right over you: as long as they do three things: when they judge they are just, when mercy is sought they show mercy, and when they covenant they fulfill. Whoever of them does not do that, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people."
"20044","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Shu'bah informed us, from Ali ibn Zayd who said: I heard al-Mughirah ibn Abi Barzah narrate from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ghifar, may Allah forgive them, and Aslam, may Allah grant them safety. I did not say it, but Allah, the Blessed and Exalted, said it."
"20045","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Abd al-Salam Abu Talut narrated to us, al-Abbas al-Jurayri narrated to us, that Ubaydullah ibn Ziyad said to Abu Barzah: Did you hear the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ever mention it, meaning the Hawd? He said: Yes, not once nor twice. Whoever denies it, may Allah not give him to drink from it."
"20046","Abd al-Samad and Yunus narrated to us, they said: Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us, from al-Azraq ibn Qays, that Sharik ibn Shihab said, Yunus said: al-Harithi, and this is the hadith of Abd al-Samad, he said: Would that I saw a man from the Companions of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who would narrate to me about the Khawarij. He said: I met Abu Barzah among some of the Companions of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Narrate to me something you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the Khawarij. He said: I will narrate to you something my ears heard and my eyes saw. Dinars were brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he distributed them, and there was a man with trimmed hair, dark or black, with a mark of prostration between his eyes, wearing two white garments. He would come to him from his right and confront him, but he gave him nothing. He said: O Muhammad, you were not just today in the division. He became intensely angry, then said: By Allah, you will not find after me anyone more just toward you than me, three times. Then he said: There will come out from the east men of whom this one was a type, their guidance is like this: they recite the Quran but it does not pass their throats, they pass through the religion as the arrow passes through the game, then they do not return to it. Their mark is shaving. They will continue to come out until the last of them comes out with the Dajjal. When you meet them, kill them. They are the worst of creation and creatures."
"20047","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, al-Azraq ibn Qays informed us, from Sharik ibn Shihab who said: I used to wish to meet a man from the Companions of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who would narrate to me about the Khawarij. I met Abu Barzah on the day of Arafah among some of his companions, and he mentioned the hadith."
"20048","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Kinanah ibn Nu'aym, from Abu Barzah, that Julaybib was from the Ansar, and the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when one of them had an unmarried woman, would not marry her off until they knew whether the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had any need concerning her or not. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said one day to a man from the Ansar: Marry your daughter to me. He said: Gladly and the delight of my eye. He said to him: I do not want her for myself. He said: For whom? He said: For Julaybib. He said: Until I consult her mother. He went to her and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) proposes your daughter. She said: Gladly and the delight of my eye, marry the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: He does not want her for himself. She said: For whom? He said: For Julaybib. She said: May she be bereaved, Julaybib, fie, twice, no, by Allah, I will not marry Julaybib. He said: When her father stood to go to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the girl said to her mother from behind her curtain: Who proposed me to you? She said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She said: Do you then reject the command of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? Hand me over to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), for he will not let me be lost. Her father went to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Deal with her accordingly, so he married her to Julaybib. While the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in one of his campaigns, and Allah, the Blessed and Exalted, granted him booty, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you miss anyone? They said: We miss so-and-so and we miss so-and-so. The Prophet said: But I miss Julaybib, so look for him among the slain. They looked and found him beside seven whom he had killed and who then killed him. He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood over him and said: He killed seven and then they killed him, this one is of me and I am of him. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) carried him on his forearms, he had no bed other than the forearms of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), until a grave was dug for him. Then he placed him in his niche grave, and no washing was mentioned."
"20049","Hajjaj narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Sayyar ibn Salamah who said: I and my father entered upon Abu Barzah and asked him about the time of the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: He used to pray Zuhr when the sun declined, and Asr when a man would return to the farthest part of Madinah while the sun was still alive, and Maghrib, Sayyar said: I forgot it, and Isha, he did not mind delaying it until a third of the night. He did not like sleep before it nor talk after it. He used to pray Subh and a man would finish and recognize the face of his companion, and he would recite in it between sixty and a hundred. Sayyar said: I do not know whether in one of the two rak'ahs or in both."
"20050","Ya'la narrated to us, al-Hajjaj ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Abu Hashim, from Rufay' Abu al-Aliyah, from Abu Barzah al-Aslami who said: Latterly, when he sat in a sitting and wanted to stand, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would say: Glory be to You, O Allah, and with Your praise, I bear witness that there is no god but You, I seek Your forgiveness and repent to You. They said: O Messenger of Allah, you now say words you did not used to say before. He said: This is an expiation for what occurs in the sitting."
"20051","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Jamil ibn Murrah, from Abu al-Wadi' who said: We were on a journey with Abu Barzah, and Abu Barzah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The two sellers have the choice as long as they have not parted."
"20052","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from Matar, from Abdullah ibn Buraydah al-Aslami who said: Ubaydullah ibn Ziyad doubted concerning the Hawd, so he sent for Abu Barzah al-Aslami and he came to him. The companions of Ubaydullah said to him: The amir only sent for you to ask you about the Hawd, did you hear anything from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mention it: whoever denies it, may Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, not give him to drink from it."
